      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a pretty strong claim. I've seen some articles recently that suggest those McKinsey-style studies might be flawed because they don't account for other variables, and that the \"diversity premium\" might not actually exist when you dig into the data. If I'm presenting this to a skeptical board, how do I address the argument that these programs are actually just a distraction from core meritocratic principles that drive growth?",
